Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.14$ | $0.16$ | $0.05$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.26$ | $0.34$ | $0.05$ | $0.65$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.5$ | $0.1$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=1,Y=1)=f(1,1)=0.26.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1)=0.65\\cdot 0.4=0.26.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Checking some possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,1) & =0.14=0.35\\cdot 0.4={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & ✓ \\\\ f(0,2) & =0.16\\ne 0.35\\cdot 0.5={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534570 17592186045417 true] [17592186426031 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426029 13194139534570 17592186045417 true] [17592186426031 1069 "q-143322" 13194139534570 17592186045417 true] [17592186426031 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534570 17592186045417 true] [17592186426031 1071 "The marginal mass functions of the independent discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are shown below. Given that the corresponding joint probability mass function is $f(x,y),$ find $f(2,3).$\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.45$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.55$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.35$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th></tr></tbody></table>" 13194139534570 17592186045417 true] [17592186426031 1072 #uuid "651363c2-d60f-536f-b27c-718f157b1a2e" 13194139534570 17592186045417 true] [17592186426031 1074 "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, since our discrete random variables are independent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(2,3) & ={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(3) \\\\  & =0.45\\cdot 0.1 \\\\  & =0.045.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534570 17592186045417 true] [17592186426032 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426028 13194139534570 17592186045417 true] [17592186426032 1069 "q-162748" 13194139534570 17592186045417 true] [17592186426032 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534570 17592186045417 true] [17592186426032 1071 "The partially complete joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the independent discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $∗$ | $0.27$ | $∗$ |\n| $X=4$ | $∗$ | $0.63$ | $?$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.1$ | $0.9$ | $1$ |\n\nWhat is the value of $P(X=4)?$" 13194139534570 17592186045417 true] [17592186426032 1072 #uuid "7688226a-1fb3-5c5e-91e0-335b33e89079" 13194139534570 17592186045417 true] [17592186426032 1074 "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, since our random variables are independent, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4,3) & ={f}_{X}(4)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(3) \\\\ P(X=4,Y=3) & =P(X=4)\\cdot P(Y=3) \\\\ 0.63 & =P(X=4)\\cdot 0.9 \\\\ P(X=4) & =\\frac{0.63}{0.9} \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534570 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-06c92b0a-61b4-5594-b403-a783ebf302b0" 17592186426012 "answer-35d0e937-69b0-5161-a9a6-fe8f1afc1e3b" 17592186426013 "answer-4e5ad509-f222-57cf-aad1-961225cbf678" 17592186426014 "answer-5508fabb-0eb4-563a-a165-699a00a19333" 17592186426015 "answer-5b911094-79ad-5c4b-8e98-e1c05675311b" 17592186426016 "answer-978e8b91-acdf-5f00-b9cf-b08102629cf8" 17592186426017 "answer-a85abc28-bebf-5356-a329-7418bb137233" 17592186426018 "answer-b3aa464a-8540-50ee-b183-67dfed5bc276" 17592186426019 "answer-b8aaee82-10a0-576b-a803-30f120b8e662" 17592186426020 "answer-b8c39168-7bf4-5d81-8f3c-f185d6fd3184" 17592186426021 "answer-c53c6d54-88b6-5bc6-af5f-adb4044c9785" 17592186426022 "answer-cd685fc2-72f4-505e-8029-94e112daad97" 17592186426023 "answer-cdce0311-011d-5bd2-b5d8-ec1a93c92eed" 17592186426024 "answer-e5d5448c-2f3a-5e0e-ab55-15065459a283" 17592186426025 "answer-ef75c0fc-986f-53cf-8094-ba198441cb7d" 17592186426026 "answer-field-2733d11c-ea48-531a-9530-4eab521f3e93" 17592186426027 "answer-field-660270d9-d112-53f6-9d24-bfc97577f56b"